*  L_ONE_driver - drives L_ONE.sno, the compiler for the language L1 (Gimpel
*  p. 411), and with it the S(NAME) and S_(NAME) functions the manifest names
*  for this module.  L1 statements are read from the input stream and the
*  assembly language for machine M (Gimpel p. 407) goes to OUTPUT.
*
*  L_ONE.sno carries its own END, so a driver can only be the include plus its
*  data; the cases therefore live in L_ONE_driver.input, which the scorecard
*  feeds on stdin by the <base>.input convention.
*
*  Per the module's own header, the left recursion in TERM and E was removed
*  for SPITBOL, which makes the operators RIGHT-associative -- so A = B/C/D
*  must be written A = (B/C)/D.  The data below respects that.
-INCLUDE "L_ONE.sno"
